	abstract = {Although Roche lobe overflow scenarios are usually quoted in relation with barium stars the authors show that a wind accretion model is better suited for explaining the barium phenomenon. This model assumes that barium stars result from the accretion of part of the matter ejected through a wind and a planetary nebula by a heavy element-rich asymptotic giant branch star, the system remaining always detached. In this first, exploratory study, a very simple, semi-analytical algorithm is used. The results of the model are applied to the system ζ Capricorni, for which a relatively good agreement is found.},
